The question asks: A number will be randomly selected from A. What is the probability that the randomly selected number will be an element of C and an element of B?

The student understands that probability = good outcomes / total outcomes, but is confused about which numbers are the "good outcomes" - they need to find numbers that are in BOTH B and C.

The key insight is that the student needs to find the intersection of B and C (numbers in both sets).

